Root cause found and fixed.

### Root cause
The board linker script at:

`examples/stm32/f4/stm32f4-discovery/stm32f4-discovery.ld`

had its final include line removed:

```ld
INCLUDE cortex-m-generic.ld
```

That include pulls in the common section/layout definitions needed by the final link step. Without it, link-time failures occur even though `miniblink/` itself is unchanged.

### Fix applied
I restored the missing line to `stm32f4-discovery.ld` directly under:

```ld
/* Include the common ld script. */
```

### Verification
Rebuilt from a clean state:

- `make clean && make V=1` in `examples/stm32/f4/stm32f4-discovery/miniblink`
- Build now completes successfully, producing `miniblink.elf`
- `git status --short` is clean after the fix (no remaining diff)

This resolves the linker failure at its source (shared board-level linker script), not in `miniblink` itself.
